   9: # description:
  10: # In the input you will see a grid with a single coloured pixel.
  11: # To make the output, move the colored pixel down one pixel and draw a yellow line from the pixel to the top of the grid.
  12: # Finally repeat the yellow line by repeating it horizontally left/right with a period of 2 pixels.
  13: 
  14: def main(input_grid):
  15:     """
  16:     Move the single colored marker down one row and draw alternating yellow columns above it.
  17: 
  18:     Input structure:
  19:     - The input is a black grid with exactly one non-black, non-yellow marker pixel.
  20:     - The marker is not on the bottom row.
  21:     - The marker's column defines the parity of the stripe pattern.
  22: 
  23:     Rule:
  24:     - Move the marker color one row downward and clear its original cell.
  25:     - From the top through the marker's original row, color yellow every other column aligned with the marker column.
  26:     - Leave all other cells black.
